From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] dyld.h: define DYLD_EXCLAVEKIT_UNAVAILABLE

The published include/mach-o/dyld.h uses DYLD_EXCLAVEKIT_UNAVAILABLE on the
NSObjectFileImage and NSModule declarations, but the block that defines it
sits inside the header's __OPEN_SOURCE__ scrub and was removed from the
tarball. The SDK's copy defines it empty for every platform but ExclaveKit;
do the same when nothing else has.

Rebase-risk: low (three lines).
---
--- a/include/mach-o/dyld.h
+++ b/include/mach-o/dyld.h
@@ -39,6 +39,10 @@
  #define DYLD_DRIVERKIT_UNAVAILABLE __API_UNAVAILABLE(driverkit)
 #else
  #define DYLD_DRIVERKIT_UNAVAILABLE
+#endif
+
+#ifndef DYLD_EXCLAVEKIT_UNAVAILABLE
+ #define DYLD_EXCLAVEKIT_UNAVAILABLE
 #endif
 
 
